{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790993590,"nonce":"SJlkfuJ+1zXil0TVETamw6JzYJs=","title":"Hybrid mode: Blinc signals stop taking writes partway through ashui's smoke test","message":"Under --mode hybrid (the default), ashui's smoke test fails one check that interp and jit pass on the same build: after some point in the run, a Blinc signal set from Haxe (SignalBool.set -\u003e hl_blinc_signal_set_bool) is followed by a get of the old value, and a computed that reads those signals never changes. Even a signal made fresh at that point (Signal.make(false); set(true); get()) reads false. The values read as the type's default, as if the handle's slot were empty (state_of returning None) rather than holding a stale value.\n\nReproducer, tracked in ashui at 2e25409: tests/fixtures/ash/hybrid_signal/run.sh builds tests/Smoke.hx and runs it in each mode:\n\n    interp: ALL PASSED\n    hybrid: FAIL focus-visible: and disabled: follow focus and the disabled state ... 1 FAILED\n    jit: ALL PASSED\n\nA second trigger, found first and worked around in ashui: LayoutTree.order() reached its native (blinc_tree_order, which only reads the layout tree and writes u64 ids into an hl.Bytes) through a closure passed to a helper, `ids((out, capacity) -\u003e LayoutTreeNative.blinc_tree_order(this.ptr, root.id, out, capacity))`. Under hybrid, right after the first such call, every signal set stopped taking; interp and jit were fine. Calling the native directly, not through the closure, made that point pass, but the run still breaks later at the check above. Neither reproduced in a small standalone program, even with order() called 10000 times to make it hot, so it seems to need the state the smoke run builds up.\n\nNot yet known whether it is tiering (a compiled function mishandling a native call's arguments or results), or the collector freeing handle blocks that are still referenced. ashui's handles are hl.Abstract blocks with finalizers; flush drops the Blinc values of handles collected since the last flush.","files":null}]}